:name: E1M-X V2N (Renesas RZ/V2N) M33-SM smoke
:description: Boot a single headless Cortex-M33 (M33-SM) Zephyr slice, no hardware.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-sim headless boot.  `tan renode` (tan-cli, crates/tan-core/src/
# renode.rs -> build_renode_argv) injects `$elf` (the resolved
# zephyr.elf) and `$repl` (this platform descriptor) via
# `renode -e "$elf=@..."` BEFORE this script runs; the `?=` defaults
# only apply when still unset, so the wrapper's values win and the
# script also runs by hand from the SDK root:
#
#     renode metadata/renode/renesas_rzv2n.resc
#
# The M33-SM is HEADLESS -- no UART console (see the .repl header), so
# there is no `showAnalyzer` here; the firmware's console lives in the
# `ram_console_buf` RAM ring.  The `--sim-mode` gateway generates its
# OWN boot .resc and streams that RAM console to a TCP socket; this
# file just boots.  NB the gateway is NOT ported yet (tan-cli#77) --
# its Python helpers went with the west command in ADR-0020 Phase 4,
# so nothing in any repo generates that boot .resc today.
#
# NOTE: because this core is headless, the plain (non --sim-mode)
# `tan renode` path produces NO console output on V2N -- its --log
# will be empty and `--expect`/log-grep won't match.  Use --sim-mode to
# observe the ram_console.
#
# NOTE: this descriptor does NOT seed `cpu VectorTableOffset`, unlike
# alif_ensemble_e8.resc (#947).  The .repl header notes the RZ/V2N M33
# needs its Secure VTOR seeded on Renode v1.16.x just as the M55 does,
# so the same guessed-offset failure is reachable here for a non-lowest-
# vaddr link shape -- but no V2N image of that shape has been run to
# confirm it, and this file feeds the REQUIRED `renode · V2N101
# --sim-mode socket contract` context, so the change is not made blind.
# Tracked as #958; do not copy the AEN fix here without a real run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
$repl ?= @metadata/renode/renesas_rzv2n.repl
$elf  ?= @examples/peripheral-io/hello-world/build/m33_sm-zephyr/zephyr/zephyr.elf

mach create "v2n101"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

sysbus LoadELF $elf

start
